*** Keywords ***
General_SiSo_Auto_SEC_CB006017_Root_access_disable_on_RU_check
    [Documentation]    Purpose of this test is to verify that root access is disabled on RMOD after
    ...                changing actSyncToRU parameter to true. Additionally it checks if it is possible
    ...                to execute root-restricted command on RMOD using sudo command.
    ...                Args: ${rmod_id} - configuration  ID of RMOD to be tested
    [Arguments]        ${rmod_id}
    ${bts_type}=                                  hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    Create admin session with default alias       bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${connection}=                                connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                           bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${mrbts_id}=                                  admin_info_model.get_mrbts_id_admin
    ...                                           connection=${connection}
    Robot Log Operation                           Changing actSyncToRU parameter value to true
    delta_configurator.set_parameter_via_delta_recommissioning
    ...                                           dist_name=MRBTS-${mrbts_id}/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/SECADM-1
    ...                                           parameter=actSyncToRU
    ...                                           value=true
    rsc_ops.update_credentials_for_all_serial_console_connections
    ...                                           password=${SYNC_TO_RU_PASSWORD}

    Robot Log Operation                           Checking if root access is disabled on RMOD-${rmod_id}
    ${output}=                                    rmod_operations.execute_ssh_command
    ...                                           rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                           command=whoami
    ...                                           connection=${connection}
    ...                                           switch_to_rfsw_user=${False}
    Should Not Contain                            ${output}     root

    Robot Log Operation                           Trying to create .txt file on RMOD-${rmod_id} using sudo
    ${output}=                                    rmod_operations.execute_ssh_command
    ...                                           rmod_id=${rmod_id}
    ...                                           command="sudo touch /tmp/test.txt"
    ...                                           connection=${connection}
    ...                                           switch_to_rfsw_user=${False}
    ...                                           custom_password=${SYNC_TO_RU_PASSWORD}
    Should Not Contain                            ${output}     Permission denied
